,title,link,text,language,family
0,Tanoan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanoan_languages,"Tanoan has long been recognized as a major family of Pueblo languages, consisting of Tiwa, Tewa, and Towa. The inclusion of Kiowa into the family was at first controversial given the cultural differences between those groups.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
1,Tewa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tewa_language,"Tewa has a fairly large phoneme inventory with 45 distinct individual sounds. Twelve of these are vowels, which can be either long or short. Tewa, like other Tanoan languages, also makes use of tones, of which it has four.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
2,Kiowa-Tanoan Language Family - EBSCO,https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/language-and-linguistics/kiowa-tanoan-language-family,"The Kiowa-Tanoan language family comprises four distinct languages: Kiowa, Tiwa, Tewa, and Towa. The Kiowa language is primarily associated with the Kiowa people, a Plains tribe residing in southwestern Oklahoma.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
3,Kiowa-Tanoan: A Synchronic and Diachronic Study,https://digitalrepository.unm.edu/ling_etds/34/,"Jul 1, 2014 · The modern constituent members of the family are Kiowa, Rio Grande Tewa, Arizona Tewa, Picuris Northern Tiwa, Taos Northern Tiwa, Southern Tiwa, and Towa. The dissertation is divided into three parts, plus a concluding discussion.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
4,Two Kiowa Songs - YouTubeKiowa-Tanoan Language Family - EBSCOTewa language - WikipediaKiowa-Tanoan languages - Academic KidsKiowa-Tanoan: A Synchronic and Diachronic StudyDelores Harragarra Collection - Sam Noble Museum,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tajaOUtFx1M,"May 26, 2011 · ""Kiowa Round Dance & Kiowa Medium Fast War Dance"" from the album Traditional Voices - Historic Recordings of Native American Music by William Koomsa Sr. & Kiowa Singers courtesy Canyon... The Kiowa-Tanoan language family comprises four distinct languages: Kiowa, Tiwa, Tewa, and Towa. The Kiowa language is primarily associated with the Kiowa people, a Plains tribe residing in southwestern Oklahoma. Tewa has a fairly large phoneme inventory with 45 distinct individual sounds. Twelve of these are vowels, which can be either long or short. Tewa, like other Tanoan languages, also makes use of tones, of which it has four. Most of the languages—Tiwa, Tewa, and Towa—are spoken in the Pueblos of New Mexico and called collectively Tanoan, while Kiowa is spoken in mostly southwestern Oklahoma. Jul 1, 2014 · The modern constituent members of the family are Kiowa, Rio Grande Tewa, Arizona Tewa, Picuris Northern Tiwa, Taos Northern Tiwa, Southern Tiwa, and Towa. The dissertation is divided into three parts, plus a concluding discussion. The collection features over 200 hours of audio recordings documenting nine languages within the Algonquian, Athabaskan, Kiowa-Tanoan and Siouan-Catawban language families.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
5,Kiowa-Tanoan languages - Academic Kids,https://aids.academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/Kiowa-Tanoan_languages,"Most of the languages—Tiwa, Tewa, and Towa—are spoken in the Pueblos of New Mexico and called collectively Tanoan, while Kiowa is spoken in mostly southwestern Oklahoma.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
6,Kiowa-Tanoan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/3702/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..LB18FvP-dvj7XXjaadjETWkUuWLIwc4v2SOmcR9XOHg,"Kiowa-Tanoan. Kiowa kio, a language of United States.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
7,Tewa - tew (Kiowa-Tanoan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/tew/,Tewa (tew) is part of the Kiowa-Tanoan family and Kiowa-Tanoan class.,Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
8,Kiowa-Tanoan Languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/kiowa-tanoan-languages/,The Kiowa-Tanoan language family currently includes 6 languages. Kiowa: 400 speakers according to UNESCO and 1092 according to SIL. Tiwa Branch.,Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
9,Kiowa-Tanoan - definition of Kiowa-Tanoan by The Free Dictionary,https://www.thefreedictionary.com/Kiowa-Tanoan,"Kiowa-Tanoan synonyms, Kiowa-Tanoan pronunciation, Kiowa-Tanoan translation, English dictionary definition of Kiowa-Tanoan. n. An American Indian language family of New Mexico, northeast Arizona, and the southern Great Plains.",Tewa,Kiowa-Tanoan
